\DOC FULL_UNIFY_F_EVENTS_TAC

\TYPE {FULL_UNIFY_F_EVENTS_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes a goal whose conclusion is an equation between two event-list
expressions, one side containing an as-yet-undetermined event-list function, by
solving for that function and discharging the equation.

\DESCRIBE
The tactic takes no arguments. It applies to a goal whose conclusion equates
two concrete event-trace terms, built from {APPEND}, {CONS}, literal event
lists, and applications of an event-list function to program parameters, and
proves it outright:
{
   A ?- t = u
   ==========  FULL_UNIFY_F_EVENTS_TAC
}
\noindent The assumptions {A} are left untouched, since nothing remains.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, the only outcome is this one — the tactic closing the
goal — on goals of this equational event-trace form, each accompanied by a
large assumption list describing machine state, nonoverlapping conditions and
the accumulated event list.

\ENDDOC
